# M1 (B1 of the one 128-row verify block, block128-design.md section 7 stage B): card M alone through the cardm action (C2_CARDS=pair: cardm is a
# pair-shaped step), the harness optimisation/ttnn-op/m8_matmul/run_card_m.sh. Every projection of the packed verify at its four-card per-chip shape
# (attn_qkv, attn_wo, gdn_qkvzab, gdn_out, mlp w1 / w3 / w2, the LM head) is run at 128 rows (per_core_M 4) and compared BIT FOR BIT, tile by tile, with the
# two 64-row halves (the config built at M = 64: what the two-block verify runs today) and with the four 32-row tiles (the sequential engine), for both
# config variants (served: verify-trace T1 #11 attn_qkv and gate; base: the plain _64 build); then timed at 32, 64 and 128 rows, and the MLP projections
# are re-gridded at per_core_M 4 (every per_core_N candidate keeps in0_block_w, so the K order; byte-checked against the halves, the best exact one named).
# An EVIDENCE job: the only new fact is whether the 128-row bits equal the 64-row bits. The LM head is ttnn.linear with NO program config (ttnn picks one
# from M): the design's one real unknown, and the reason this job exists before any phase 2 work.
# READ: results m8matmul-<stamp>.json and the log's M8_MATMUL lines, ending 'M8_MATMUL verdict=PASS' (every projection and variant exact against both
# oracles) or FAIL. A FAIL names the projection, the variant and the 32-row tile whose bits differ: for the LM head, phase 2 pins the 64-row config; for a
# 1D config, phase 2 does not take the 128-row call for it. PASS is exactness only: timing_ok per projection and timing_total_ok are reported (the review's
# rule: t128 <= t64 + 1.5 x (t64 - t32) per projection, sum t128 <= 1.1 x sum t64), with the re-grid winner and the builder arguments that reproduce it.
# NOTHING IS APPLIED by this job. It runs one container on card M alone and never resets: the next job (Z) rescans and resets all four.
# The card-M workflow step waits for the host's buildx builders to finish before it opens the card, and refuses while card M or card A is held.
# ON A HANG (exit 124 / 137) the harness prints the one-card reset hint; Z resets all four.
# Duration (estimate): 45-60 min (about 9 projection runs, each three compiles and three timings, plus up to 48 re-grid candidates; container timeout 60 min).
# Stop rule: a failure stops the window (there is nothing after Z to run, and Z heals the cards).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/m8-phase1 one-card window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/m8-phase1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1 is the image the tp4/262k8 development window built and left on the rig; this window builds nothing. The harness mounts
# THIS checkout's scripts (m8_matmul_bytes.py, m8_matmul_plan.py and the sweep modules they import) into that image, so a commit of those files needs no
# new image. The cards are under development and production is down by the owner's choice: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/m8_matmul/run_card_m.sh
C2_CARDM_ENV=IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1
